obs Reviewed the card, Bakery prompt, newest three shelf logs, handoffs, roster, and live claims. Copal owns its bounds control, Pheromone its Glow recovery, and Diffuser its motion study. The claim reader reported overlap_peer=0 and commits_behind=0. This review opens no instrument or booked repair.
obs Round-open settled at 6af36954d874bee62ffe0d4705469a49e3c2a224; the full lap-open hash is retained in session-output/bakery-code-audit-head. All 85 stashes remain preserved. The fleet process reader found no local roster runner and refused foreign checkouts.
obs Audited source changes in each stash working tree and index against its first parent, plus files in its untracked third parent. Selected suffixes were .sh, .rye, .rish, .py, .brix, .swift, .c, .h, and .zig. Deduplicated by path, mode, and blob. Generated .tpr copies and prose are outside this source census.
loom parked_source_audit stashes=85 distinct_versions=176 matching_head=13 differing_at_existing_path=145 missing_head_versions=18
obs Compared those tuples against raw ancestor diffs at the same path, retaining modes and both sides of each diff. Sixty-seven additional versions occur in that history. Ninety-six lack that exact historical match; that alone says nothing about whether their behavior later landed in different bytes.
loom parked_source_history current=13 historical_at_path=67 needs_semantic_review=96
obs The 18 missing-path versions cover 15 distinct paths. The path-absence reader fetched xy and found all 15 absent both locally and upstream, with commits_behind=0 and verdict=absent. Some may have moved or been superseded; path absence alone does not justify restoration.
obs Reviewed stash 336cfe84ab83605d21db3db03916649caaee0e86, parked September 21. Its four Caravan source changes add a rights count, a next_hop helper, a check_chain_bound self-test, a witness output assertion, and a carry census adjustment. HEAD retains the pre-patch bytes for all four paths.
obs The parked next_hop helper has exactly two call sites, both inside check_chain_bound. The self-test only decrements an integer. It constructs no capabilities and performs no confer_word transfer. No production path carries hops_remaining. Restoring this patch would claim an enforced chain limit that the runtime does not enforce.
obs The patch's strict-narrowing premise also needs redesign. confer_word starts granted at ceiling and clears only right_write for a read request; an r-only ceiling remains r. The existing check_words case renders menu:r, and the declaration grants client_a menu r. The current Caravan confer witness passed on this host. This checks the existing implementation, not an onward chain or the parked counter.
obs Diffuser's September 18 proposal explicitly leaves same-mask transfers open. A future bound needs a chosen rule for those transfers, a counter carried and checked through the real transfer path, and acceptance/refusal tests using actual transfers. Five rights bounds strict removals; it does not by itself bound arbitrary transfers. The dated proposal and stash remain unchanged.
obs Reviewed the parked wrap-ring witness as well: HEAD keeps its private session-output directory and one shell trap across build and proof. Restoring the older witness would regress that cleanup. Ninety-one other unmatched versions still need semantic review; no claim of complete recovery is made.
obs The census is saved in session-output/bakery-code-audit.json and the absence reading in session-output/bakery-code-absence.txt. These are local working receipts. The durable findings and source stash identifier live in this log.
obs The current ancestor timeout is 5400 seconds. The prior measured cold/hot/cadence estimate remains 9837 seconds before overhead. Full roster passes were not launched in this review; full cold, cadence, and full hot remain owed. No roster process is left running across the lap boundary.
obs Focused checks passed: current Caravan confer, index-row-bound including 39 repair-control behaviors, and parent-nib including its refusal case. All four touched records grade A+; the card grade checks cited paths, and the changed card claims were reviewed separately. These checks establish no full-roster verdict.
rota lap 6569, row 4 -- Earth - Mercury; a stored blob proves what was written. Its calls and data fields decide whether the claimed bound reaches a real transfer.
